{:edb/db-before-t 1796 :edb/db-after-t 1797 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535109 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:04:51.537Z" 13194139535109 true] [17592186128867 1100 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{2x+20}[/math]}} \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+12x+25\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-\\,\\,8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{20x+25}[/math]}} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{20x-80}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,105 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535109 true] [17592186128867 1100 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$[math]\\phantom{2x+20}[/math]; x - 42x^{2} + 12x + 25; 2x^{2} - 8x_(―); 4x^{2} -[math]\\phantom{20x+25}[/math]; 4x^{2} -20x - 80_(―); 4x^{2} + 26x105$" 13194139535109 false] [17592186128867 1145 "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n2x + 20; x - 42x^{2} + 12x + 25; 2x^{2} - 8x_(―); 4x^{2} -20x + 25; 4x^{2} -20x - 80_(―); 4x^{2} + 26x105\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are $2x+20$ and $20x+25$." 13194139535109 false] [17592186128867 1145 "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+20 \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+12x+25\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-\\,\\,8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20x+25 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{20x-80}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,105 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are $2x+20$ and $20x+25.$" 13194139535109 true] [17592186128868 1100 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x^2 - x + 1}[/math]}} \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x + 64}[/math]}} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535109 true] [17592186128868 1100 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$x + 1[math]\\phantom{x^2 - x + 1}[/math]; x + 1x^{3} + 0x^{2} + 0x + 64; x + 1x^{3} + 0x^{2}_(―); x + 1x^{3}- 0x^{2} + 0x + 64; x + 1x^{3}- 0x^{2} - 0x_(―); x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} -[math]\\phantom{x + 64}[/math]; x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} -x + 11_(―); x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} + x -63$" 13194139535109 false] [17592186128868 1145 "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^2$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\nx^3+{\\color{red}0}x^2 + {\\color{red}0}x + 64\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-x+1 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\qquad$ $x^2 - x + 1\\quad$ and $\\quad x + 64.$" 13194139535109 true] [17592186128868 1145 "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^2$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\nx^3+{\\color{red}0}x^2 + {\\color{red}0}x + 64\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$x + 1x^{2} - x + 1; x + 1x^{3} + 0x^{2} + 0x + 64; x + 1x^{3} + 0x^{2}_(―); x + 1x^{3}- 0x^{2} + 0x + 64; x + 1x^{3}- 0x^{2} - 0x_(―); x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} -x + 64; x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} -x + 11_(―); x + 1x^{3} - x^{2} + x -63$\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\qquad$ $x^2 - x + 1\\quad$ and $\\quad x + 64$." 13194139535109 false] [17592186128870 1100 "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-2 \\\\  & x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+8x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, what is $\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5}?$" 13194139535109 true] [17592186128870 1100 "Consider the following polynomial division:\n$x + 22x - 2; x + 52x^{2} + 18x - 15; x + 22x^{2} + 10x- 15_(―); x + 23x^{2}- 12x - 15; x + 23x^{2}- 12x - 10_(―); x + 23x^{2} - 2x -15$\n\nFrom the above, what is $\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5}$?" 13194139535109 false] [17592186128870 1145 "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-2 \\\\  & x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+8x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $2x^2+8x -5$ by the linear binomial ${\\color{purple}x+5}$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${\\color{blue}2x-2},$ and\n\n- the remainder ${\\color{red}5}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5} = {\\color{blue}2x-2}+\\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{purple}x+5}.\n$$" 13194139535109 true] [17592186128870 1145 "$$\nx + 22x - 2; x + 52x^{2} + 18x - 15; x + 22x^{2} + 10x- 15_(―); x + 23x^{2}- 12x - 15; x + 23x^{2}- 12x - 10_(―); x + 23x^{2} - 2x -15\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $2x^2+8x -5$ by the linear binomial ${\\color{purple}x+5}$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${\\color{blue}2x-2}$, and\n- the remainder ${\\color{red}5}$.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5} = {\\color{blue}2x-2}+\\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{purple}x+5}\n$$" 13194139535109 false] [17592186129052 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331767 13194139535109 true] [17592186129052 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331774 13194139535109 true] [17592186129052 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331781 13194139535109 true] [17592186129052 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331821 13194139535109 true] [17592186129053 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331795 13194139535109 true] [17592186129053 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331802 13194139535109 true] [17592186129053 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331828 13194139535109 true] [17592186129053 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331842 13194139535109 true] [17592186129055 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331788 13194139535109 true] [17592186129055 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331809 13194139535109 true] [17592186129055 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331815 13194139535109 true] [17592186129055 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331835 13194139535109 true] [17592186129339 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535109 true] [17592186129339 1100 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 3x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+4x+3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535109 true] [17592186129339 1100 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$2x + 2; 3x - 16x^{2} + 4x + 3; 6x^{2} - 2x_(―); 6x^{2} +6x + 3; 6x^{2} +6x - 2_(―); 6x^{2} + 4x +5$" 13194139535109 false] [17592186129339 1145 "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+2 \\\\  & 3x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+4x+3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $2x+2\\,$ and $\\,6x-2.$" 13194139535109 true] [17592186129342 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535109 true] [17592186129342 1100 "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+3x+9 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{9x-27}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{{x}^{3}-1}{x-3}=$" 13194139535109 true] [17592186129342 1100 "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$x - 3x^{2} + 3x + 9; x - 3x^{3} + 0x^{2} + 0x - 01; x - 3x^{3} - 3x^{2}_(―); x - 3x^{3} -3x^{2} + 0x - 01; x - 3x^{3} -3x^{2} - 9x_(―); x - 3x^{3} - 0x^{2} +9x - 01; x - 3x^{3} - 0x^{2} +9x - 27_(―); x - 3x^{3} - 0x^{2} + 0x -26$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{x^{3} - 1}{x - 3} =$" 13194139535109 false] [17592186129342 1145 "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+3x+9 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\